      </ul>
      <h3 id="cpmso-feat-auto-update_cpmso-managing-machines" class="group scroll-mt-20">Automatic updates to the control plane configuration<a href="#cpmso-feat-auto-update_cpmso-managing-machines" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <p>The <code>RollingUpdate</code> update strategy automatically propagates changes to your control plane configuration to minimize manual intervention. {"{"}._abstract{"}"} This update strategy is the default configuration for the control plane machine set.</p>
      <p>For clusters that use the <code>RollingUpdate</code> update strategy, the Operator creates a replacement control plane machine with the configuration that is specified in the CR. When the replacement control plane machine is ready, the Operator deletes the control plane machine that is marked for replacement. The replacement machine then joins the control plane.</p>
      <p>If multiple control plane machines are marked for replacement, the Operator protects etcd health during replacement by repeating this replacement process one machine at a time until it has replaced each machine.</p>
